# Sports Tournament Database – Phase 1

## Overview
This project is a sports tournament management system implemented using a relational database.

The purpose of Phase 1 is to design the database structure, including entities, attributes, and relationships, using ERD and relational schema (DSD).

---

## System Description
The system manages a sports tournament that includes:
- National teams
- Players
- Matches
- Stadiums
- Match events
- Referees
- Coaches

The database allows tracking of players, teams, matches, and events that occur during matches.

---

## ERD (Entity Relationship Diagram)

The ERD describes the main entities and their relationships.

### Main Entities:
- Player
- NationalTeam
- Match
- Stadium
- MatchEvent
- Referee
- Coach
- PlayerStatistics

### Key Relationships:
- A team has many players (1:N)
- A team has one coach (1:1)
- A match includes many events (1:N)
- A player participates in events (1:N)
- A match is officiated by a referee (1:N)
- Matches are played in stadiums

---

## DSD (Database Schema Design)

### Player
- player_id (PK)
- first_name
- last_name
- birth_date
- jersey_number
- position
- height
- nationality
- team_id (FK)
- extra_info_json

### NationalTeam
- team_id (PK)
- team_name
- country
- team_rank
- sport_type
- founded_date
- team_colors
- team_details_json

### Match
- match_id (PK)
- match_date
- home_team
- away_team
- home_score
- away_score
- attendance
- status
- stadium_id (FK)

### Stadium
- stadium_id (PK)
- stadium_name
- city
- country
- capacity
- build_date
- stadium_type

### MatchEvent
- event_id (PK)
- match_id (FK)
- event_type
- event_minute
- event_description
- event_data_json
- severity_level

### Referee
- referee_id (PK)
- first_name
- last_name
- birth_date
- nationality
- certification_level
- years_of_experience

### Coach
- coach_id (PK)
- first_name
- last_name
- birth_date
- nationality
- contract_start_date
- years_of_experience

### PlayerStatistics
- stat_id (PK)
- player_id (FK)
- match_id (FK)
- stat_date
- points_or_goals
- assists
- fouls
- yellow_cards
- red_cards
- minutes_played

---

## Design Decisions

- Primary keys are numeric for performance and simplicity.
- Foreign keys are used to maintain relationships between tables.
- JSON fields are used for flexible and dynamic data (extra_info_json, event_data_json).
- Some derived values (like number_of_players) may be calculated dynamically in later phases.

---

## Assumptions

- Each player belongs to exactly one team.
- Each team has one coach.
- Each match has one referee.
- Each match takes place in one stadium.
- Events are always linked to a match.

---

## Files Included

- ERD diagram (image)
- DSD schema
- Documentation file (this README)

